## 4. Frontend: Chatbot Input UX Enhancements

We improved the conversational input interface to resolve focus loss issues and improve readability/positioning for long user messages.

### Changes Made

- **[TryPragyaChat.tsx](file:///c:/Users/JAKKOJU/Downloads/app-heyattrangi/app-heyattrangi/components/ai-bot/TryPragyaChat.tsx)**:
  - **Focus Retention**: Introduced an `inputRef` declaration and registered a React `useEffect` callback watching `isLoading` / `isTyping` changes. This triggers auto-focus on the input element immediately when the bot completes responding or typing. Refocused when suggestion pills are accepted.
  - **Premium Flexbox Container Layout**: Refactored the form wrapper to use a flex layout with `items-end` alignment. The rounded borders, shadow effects, and focus outlines are styled directly on the containing `form` wrapper itself.
  - **Borderless expanding textarea**: The `<textarea>` runs borderless and transparent inside the flex container. Its height grows dynamically (`min-h-[44px]` up to `max-h-[160px]`) as the user types long paragraphs, wrapping properly.
  - **Send Button Alignment**: Positioned the send button next to the textarea as a flex sibling (`shrink-0 mb-1`), aligning it automatically at the bottom-right corner without overlapping or obscuring any text.

### Verification Results

Verify the behavior in the browser:

- Focus: Sending a message focuses the cursor back in the text box immediately upon completion of typewriter response streaming.
- Submissions: Sending via `Enter` works, while `Shift + Enter` starts a new line.
- Dynamic Height: Long inputs wrap and expand the text box height smoothly.
- Visual Layout: The send button sits next to the textarea, always remaining at the bottom-right corner of the container without overlapping or blocking any typed characters.
